## Details (as Reported)

- TechCrunch reported that the account of the meeting came from The Wall Street Journal ([TechCrunch](https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/24/in-all-hands-meeting-jensen-huang-thanks-white-house-and-says-hes-in-therapy/)).
- The company stated on November 23, 2026, that it "will continue to cooperate with ongoing government investigations and inquiries" ([Securities and Exchange Commission filing](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001045810/000104581026000090/nov23pressrelease.htm)).
- The company also announced a search to fill a new position, Chief Compliance Officer, which will report to the Nominating and Corporate Governance Committee ([Securities and Exchange Commission filing](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001045810/000104581026000090/nov23pressrelease.htm)).

